# Cosplay Horizons — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
# In Vercel: Project Settings → Environment Variables → add these three.
# NEVER commit real keys. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# Supabase is OPTIONAL for previewing the site. With these unset, the site
# uses the seeded local data in src/lib/data.ts (13 entries, 6 real photos).
# With them set, the site reads approved cosplays from Supabase and
# submissions / takedowns are saved to Supabase instead of only being
# acknowledged in preview mode.
#
# Get these from your Supabase project: Settings → API
#   URL = Project URL
#   ANON_KEY = anon / publishable key (safe to expose in the browser)
#   SERVICE_ROLE_KEY = service_role / secret key (SERVER ONLY — never
#   put it in NEXT_PUBLIC_* and never commit it; only the API routes use it)

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Supabase plan notes (as of Nov 2026) ---
# Free plan: 500 MB database, 1 GB file storage, 50,000 monthly active
# users, and the project PAUSES after 7 days of inactivity (you can
# un-pause it from the Supabase dashboard, but it is not always-on).
# Pro plan: $25/month — no pausing, 8 GB database, 100 GB file storage.
# For a soft launch with friends, Free is fine. Upgrade to Pro before
# a public launch, or if the site goes quiet for a week and you do not
# want it to pause.
#
# Vercel plan notes: start on Personal / Hobby (free, non-commercial
# only). Upgrade to Pro ($20/month) only when you turn on ads — Vercel
# counts ads, including AdSense, as commercial use.
